#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:1
msgid "VTK::RenderingVolumeWebGPU"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:3
msgid "Volume rendering for the WebGPU backend. Two classes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:5
msgid ""
"`vtkWebGPUVolumeRayCastMapper`, an object factory override of "
"`vtkGPUVolumeRayCastMapper` tagged with `RenderingBackend=WebGPU` so that "
"`vtkObjectFactory` preferences pick between it and the OpenGL mapper. It "
"prepares inputs; it does not draw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:9
msgid ""
"`vtkWebGPUVolumeRayCastCoordinator`, one per renderer, which gathers the "
"inputs of every volume in that renderer and marches them together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:12
msgid "Why a coordinator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:14
msgid ""
"Volume rendering only composites correctly when the volumes that share a ray "
"are sampled together. If each mapper drew its own volume in turn, each would "
"composite a finished image over the last, which is wrong wherever two "
"volumes occupy the same space and order dependent everywhere else. That is "
"the reason the OpenGL backend needs a `vtkMultiVolume` and refuses to let "
"its inputs overlap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:21
msgid ""
"Here the volumes are brought back together at the renderer instead. Adding "
"several `vtkVolume` props is enough, each with its own mapper and its own "
"transfer functions, overlapping or not. Several inputs on one mapper still "
"work and join the same pass, and so does a `vtkMultiVolume`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:26
msgid "How a frame is put together"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:28
msgid ""
"The mapper does its work across three of the stages `vtkWebGPURenderer` runs "
"through."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:0
msgid "Stage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:0
msgid "What happens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:0
msgid "`SyncDeviceResources`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:0
msgid ""
"Tabulate the transfer functions, classify the volume into cells, and offer "
"one contribution per connected port to the coordinator of the renderer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:0
msgid "`RecordingCommands`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:0
msgid "Hand the volume to `vtkWebGPURenderer::AddPostRasterizationProp`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:0
msgid "`RenderPostRasterization`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:0
msgid ""
"Whichever volume arrives first has the coordinator decide which bricks to "
"keep resident, write the uniforms, build the bind group around the finished "
"depth buffer, and record one ray casting pass for all of them. The rest find "
"the work already done."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:37
msgid ""
"The mapper keeps what belongs to one input: the tabulated transfer "
"functions, the cell classification, and the ability to hand over the voxels "
"of any one brick. The coordinator keeps what the pass shares: the brick "
"pool, the page table, the transfer function texture arrays, the cell buffer, "
"the parameter buffers, the bind group and the pipeline. A contribution "
"(`Private/vtkWebGPUVolumeRayCastContribution.h`) is how one crosses to the "
"other, and carries a time stamp so that layers and cells that did not change "
"are not uploaded again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:46
msgid ""
"Notice which way the voxels travel. The mapper never uploads a volume; it "
"answers for one brick when asked. Deciding what is worth having on the "
"device needs the camera and the memory budget, which the coordinator has and "
"the mapper does not, so residency is the coordinator's to decide and "
"fetching is the mapper's to answer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:52
msgid ""
"Settings that describe the march rather than a single volume, the blend mode "
"above all, are handled specially. When volumes do not overlap (based on "
"their bounding boxes), each can use its own blend mode. When volumes "
"overlap, they must all use the same blend mode - an error is reported if "
"they don't, since overlapping volumes with different blend modes cannot be "
"composited correctly. Everything that is genuinely per volume, including "
"clipping planes, transfer functions, and shading parameters, lives in the "
"per volume parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:60
msgid ""
"Nothing is drawn in the main render pass. That pass owns the depth "
"attachment, and the ray march has to read the depth the opaque geometry left "
"behind in order to stop rays at surfaces, which a pass cannot do with an "
"attachment it is still writing to. Waiting until the main pass has been "
"flushed also means the volumes are composited over a finished frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:66
msgid "The shader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:68
msgid "`wgsl/VolumeRayCast.wgsl` holds both stages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:70
msgid ""
"The vertex stage draws the world space box that bounds every input, keeping "
"the faces that point away from the camera so that one ray is cast per "
"covered pixel even when the camera is inside the box. When the near plane "
"cuts into the box the faces stop covering the viewport, and the mapper "
"switches to a full screen triangle instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:76
msgid ""
"The fragment stage rebuilds the ray by unprojecting the pixel at both ends "
"of the clip volume, which works for parallel and perspective cameras alike "
"and parameterises the ray by world distance from the near plane. That "
"parameter is shared by every input no matter how each one is placed, which "
"is what lets overlapping inputs be composited correctly: at each step the "
"shader collects the inputs that contain the current point, blends them as "
"media that share it, and composites the result once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:84
msgid "Bricks, and how a volume reaches the device"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:86
msgid ""
"No volume is bound as a texture of its own. Every volume is cut into bricks "
"of `vtkWebGPUVolumeRayCastCoordinator::PoolBrickSize` voxels a side, the "
"bricks that are resident live in one shared pool texture (`Private/"
"vtkWebGPUVolumeBrickPool.h`), and a page table says which pool slot holds "
"which brick. There are two pools, one for eight bit scalars and one for "
"floats, so how many volumes a pass can hold is a question about the "
"parameter buffer rather than about texture bindings, and how much data they "
"hold is a question about the pool budget rather than about any single "
"texture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:95
msgid ""
"Each slot carries a one voxel apron around its brick, taken from the brick's "
"neighbours. That is what makes the cutting invisible: the eight texels the "
"filter reaches for always land inside a single slot, so one page lookup "
"serves the whole interpolation and a brick boundary reads exactly what a "
"single large texture would have read. It is also what lets the pools be "
"filtered in hardware rather than interpolated by hand - VTK asks its WebGPU "
"device for Float32Filterable, so every format a pool uses can be sampled "
"directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:103
msgid ""
"The pool holds `BrickPoolSizeMB` megabytes at most, and grows only as far as "
"the volumes in the scene actually need. When they need more than that, the "
"bricks nearest the camera and inside the view frustum are the ones kept: "
"bricks are sorted by distance, what is already resident is claimed before "
"anything is evicted, and slots are recycled least recently used first, never "
"taking one the frame being drawn has already claimed. A brick that is not "
"resident is stepped over rather than read, and `MaximumBricksPerFrame` caps "
"how many arrive per frame, so a volume larger than the pool draws "
"immediately and fills in over the frames that follow. `GetComplete()` says "
"whether the last frame got everything it asked for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:114
msgid "Streaming, and never reading a volume whole"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:116
msgid ""
"Residency decides what is kept on the device out of a volume that has been "
"read. Streaming asks the question one stage earlier: what is worth reading "
"at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:119
msgid ""
"When the source of an input publishes "
"`vtkStreamingDemandDrivenPipeline::CAN_PRODUCE_SUB_EXTENT()` and the volume "
"is larger than the mapper's `StreamingThresholdMB`, the input is never "
"updated whole. `vtkVolume::RenderVolumetricGeometry` calls `Mapper-"
">Update()` before every render, so the mapper overrides `ProcessRequest` and "
"answers `REQUEST_UPDATE_EXTENT` for a streamed port with an empty extent, "
"which asks the pipeline for nothing. Bricks are then fetched one at a time "
"as the coordinator claims them, each by an `Update(port, requests)` over "
"that brick's extent grown by its apron."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:129
msgid ""
"What that costs is knowing the volume before reading it. The scalar range, "
"which the transfer functions are tabulated over, has to come from the "
"source's `vtkDataObject::FIELD_RANGE()` rather than from the array; without "
"one the transfer functions' own range is used and a warning is issued. Cell "
"classification cannot be done up front either, so cells start out unknown "
"and are classified as the bricks covering them arrive. An unknown cell is "
"treated as full - opacity 1, varying - so the march is conservative until it "
"knows better, and the frame after a brick lands is the one that sees its "
"cells. That is why `GetComplete()` stays false for a frame after the last "
"brick."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:139
msgid ""
"An input with a mask, a second transfer function axis array, cell scalars or "
"ghost arrays is read whole however large it is: the first two are whole "
"volumes of their own, and the last two are defined against a whole grid. A "
"mask and a second axis show in the pipeline's metadata; cell and ghost "
"arrays do not, so a single voxel is read first and what that probe finds "
"decides whether the input is streamed at all. A refusal lasts until "
"something upstream of the input changes, at which point it is asked again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:147
msgid "Interpolation, and the finished colour"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:149
msgid ""
"`vtkVolumeProperty::InterpolationType` picks between reading the nearest "
"voxel and interpolating between the eight around it. Nearest does not need a "
"sampler of its own: landing the sample exactly on a texel centre puts all of "
"the filter's weight on one texel, which is the same thing for less. Note "
"that vtkVolumeProperty starts at nearest, not at linear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:155
msgid ""
"`vtkGPUVolumeRayCastMapper::FinalColorWindow` and `FinalColorLevel` put a "
"window and level over the finished colour, as a scale of one over the window "
"and a bias of a half less the level over the window. The colour is "
"premultiplied by then, so the bias is weighed by the alpha it was multiplied "
"through by. Like the blend mode these describe the pass rather than one "
"volume, so the primary input settles them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:162
msgid "Finding empty space"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:164
msgid ""
"Where a volume is empty is a finer question than what is worth keeping on "
"the device, so it is asked at a different scale. Each input is measured in "
"cells of the mapper's `BrickSize` voxels, with a voxel of overlap so a cell "
"also covers what interpolation produces inside it. Whenever the transfer "
"functions change, every cell is classified into the largest opacity the "
"functions map it to and how much it varies, using a sparse range table over "
"the opacity table so the classification costs one lookup per cell rather "
"than a scan. The shader reads that classification to jump over cells that "
"map to nothing and to choose a step between `MinimumSampleDistanceFactor` "
"and `MaximumSampleDistanceFactor` times the base distance. The coordinator "
"reads it too: a brick is left out of the pool only when every cell in it is "
"empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:176
msgid ""
"Opacity is corrected for the distance a step actually travels, so a cell of "
"uniform material composites to the same colour however coarsely it is "
"crossed. The intensity blend modes weigh every sample equally and only mean "
"what they say when the samples are evenly spaced, so adaptive sampling is "
"bypassed for them - and so is dropping empty bricks, because those modes "
"look at the scalars rather than at what the transfer functions make of them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:183
msgid "Limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:185
msgid ""
"Twelve volumes per renderer per pass, set by how many the shared parameter "
"buffer describes. Anything beyond that is not drawn, with a warning. This is "
"a limit on how many volumes, not on how large they are."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:188
msgid ""
"Six lights per renderer, six clipping planes per volume and sixteen iso "
"values. These are the lengths of fixed arrays in the shader's uniform "
"buffers, and of the arrays a ray keeps while it marches. A scene that asks "
"for more gets the first ones, with a warning. Raising a limit means changing "
"the constant in `wgsl/VolumeRayCast.wgsl` and its twin in "
"`vtkWebGPUVolumeRayCastCoordinatorInternals.cxx`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../modules/vtk-modules/Rendering/VolumeWebGPU/README.md:194
msgid ""
"Rectilinear grids, volumetric scattering and reduced image sample distances "
"are not implemented."
msgstr ""
